## 2. Legacy-to-Target Component Mapping
| Legacy Component | Legacy Library / Pattern | Modern Target Equivalent | Advantages |
|---|---|---|---|
| Ingress Controller | Monolithic MVC Controller | Fastify / NestJS / gRPC Handler | Low latency, strict schema validation |
| Caching & Session | In-memory session / Static Map | Redis Cluster / Redis Sentinel | Horizontally scalable, zero single point of failure |
| Background Queues | Monolithic Thread / Cron | Apache Kafka / Consumer Fleet | Fault-tolerant, replayable event logs, partitioned scale |
| Concurrency Control | In-process DB row locks | Redis Distributed Mutex (Redlock) | Non-blocking database, cluster-wide safety |
| Data Access | Bloated ORM / Raw SqlClient | Clean Repository (Prisma/Drizzle/SQLX) | Type-safe, isolated database ports |

